           principal point and at most 36 px inside the image's edges.  On
           2933 of them, in the top right and bottom right corners, the
           iteration repels and gives up 19-35 px off.  The rest, there and 1
           in the top left corner, converge too slowly.  The default
           --pixel_border of 50 would drop every tag they touch, but the
           robots run with 25, so a tag reaching 25-34 px from the edges in
           the right corners is dropped when its corners don't converge, or
           refined from edge samples which didn't.  Recalibrate 25-09 and
           remove this. */
        "waived_calibrations": [
          {"camera_id": "25-09", "calibration_timestamp": 1741304224499387712}
        ],
